{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-p3-blowup-yekutieli-intro","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:p3-blowup-yekutieli-intro","kind":"prose","title":"Blowup as a finite obstruction level","text":"p3-blowup-yekutieli-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:p3-blowup-yekutieli-intro\"></a><p>One identifies finite-time Navier-Stokes (NS) blowup with a finite obstruction level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n^*</code> in the brane tower. At this level, a velocity field ceases to lift. One encodes a counter-example by the cohomological address <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(v_0, T^*, \\Sigma, n^*, \\kappa_{n^*})</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/p3-blowup-yekutieli-intro.md","heading":"","page":"b/sec-p3-blowup-yekutieli-intro","qa":{"counts":{"pass":43,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":15,"unknown":0,"stale":58}}}
